.TH JUNK 1 2026-10-18 "junk 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.\" Left-aligned and unhyphenated, so key names and paths copy as written.
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
junk \- Junk Drawer, a minimal file manager for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B junk
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.RI [ PATH | URI ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Junk Drawer
is a lightweight GTK 4 file manager with an icon view and a details view, a
sidebar of places, bookmarks and volumes, Catppuccin colours and a transparent
window background.
.PP
It opens a window on each
.I PATH
or
.I URI
given, or on your home folder when there are none.
URIs can be anything GIO understands, such as
.B sftp://host/srv
or
.BR recent:/// .
Junk Drawer runs as a single instance: when it is already running, the new windows
open in that process.
.PP
Every window, dialogs included, has the Wayland app_id
.BR io.github.DisposableSoftware.JunkDrawer ,
so compositor window rules can match it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Neither option opens a window or contacts a running Junk Drawer.
GApplication's own options, such as
.BR \-\-gapplication\-service ,
which D-Bus activation uses (see
.BR D-BUS ),
are accepted too.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
Click, Ctrl+click, Shift+click
Select an item, toggle it in the selection, or extend the selection to it.
Dragging on empty space draws a selection rectangle.
.TP
Double-click
Open the item.
A folder opens in the same window; several selected folders open in new
windows, and files open in their default applications.
.TP
Right-click
Open the context menu for the selection, or for the folder when clicking
empty space.
.TP
Back and forward thumb buttons
Go back and forward in the window's history.
.TP
Ctrl+scroll
Zoom the view in or out.
.TP
Column header (details view)
Sort by that column; click again to reverse the order.
.TP
Drag and drop
Dragging items moves them when the destination is on the same filesystem and
copies them when it is not.
Hold Ctrl to copy or Shift to move.
Drop on a folder to put the items in it, or on empty space to put them in the
current folder.
Other applications can drag files in and out.
.TP
Sidebar
Click a row to open it.
Click a volume that isn't mounted to mount it, and its eject button to eject
or unmount it.
Right-click a bookmark to remove it.
.TP
Up button
Go to the parent folder.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Each binding has a name, used in the
.B [keybindings]
group of
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/keybindings.ini
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
A
.B [keybindings]
section in
.I config.ini
is ignored, with a warning.
To change one, write the name and a list of keys separated by
.BR ; ,
for example
.BR "go\-up = <Alt>Up;BackSpace;<Ctrl>u" .
An empty value unbinds it, and a binding that isn't listed keeps its default
keys.
Keys use GTK accelerator syntax: any of
.BR <Ctrl> ,
.BR <Shift> ,
.B <Alt>
and
.B <Super>
followed by a GDK key name, such as
.BR Return ,
.BR BackSpace ,
.B F2
or
.BR question .
.PP
Keys without Ctrl, Alt or Super work wherever focus is in the window, but
never while you are typing in a text field.
Unknown names and keys that can't be parsed are reported once on standard
error and skipped.
Press
.B ?
in a window to see the bindings in effect.
.PP
The bindings and their default keys:
.TP
.B new\-window
New window.
Opens another window on the current folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>n\fR
.TP
.B close\-window
Close window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>w\fR, \fBq\fR
.TP
.B quit
Quit.
Closes every window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>q\fR
.TP
.B open
Open.
Opens the selected items, as a double-click does.
.br
Keys: \fBReturn\fR, \fBKP_Enter\fR, \fBspace\fR
.TP
.B rename
Rename.
Renames the selected item.
.br
Keys: \fBF2\fR
.TP
.B view\-icons
Icon view.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>1\fR
.TP
.B view\-details
Details view.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>2\fR
.TP
.B toggle\-hidden
Toggle hidden files.
Shows or hides dot files and backup files ending in
.BR ~ .
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>h\fR
.TP
.B go\-up
Go up.
Opens the parent folder, with the folder you came from selected.
.br
Keys: \fB<Alt>Up\fR, \fBBackSpace\fR
.TP
.B go\-back
Back.
.br
Keys: \fB<Alt>Left\fR
.TP
.B go\-forward
Forward.
.br
Keys: \fB<Alt>Right\fR
.TP
.B go\-home
Home folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Alt>Home\fR
.TP
.B reload
Reload.
.br
Keys: \fBF5\fR, \fB<Ctrl>r\fR
.TP
.B select\-all
Select all.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>a\fR
.TP
.B unselect\-all
Select none.
.br
Keys: \fBEscape\fR
.TP
.B copy
Copy.
Puts the selected files on the clipboard, for pasting here or in another
file manager.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>c\fR
.TP
.B cut
Cut.
Like copy, but pasting moves the files.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>x\fR
.TP
.B paste
Paste.
Copies or moves the files on the clipboard into the current folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>v\fR
.TP
.B trash
Move to trash.
Asks first.
In Recent, removes the items from the list instead.
.br
Keys: \fBDelete\fR
.TP
.B trash\-now
Move to trash without asking.
In Recent, removes the items from the list instead.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>Delete\fR
.TP
.B delete
Delete permanently.
Asks first.
In Recent, removes the items from the list instead.
.br
Keys: \fB<Shift>Delete\fR
.TP
.B new\-folder
New folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl><Shift>n\fR
.TP
.B open\-with
Open with.
Chooses an application for the selected files.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B properties
Properties.
Shows the selected items, or the current folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>i\fR, \fB<Alt>Return\fR
.TP
.B context\-menu
Context menu.
Opens the menu at the focused item.
.br
Keys: \fBMenu\fR, \fB<Shift>F10\fR
.TP
.B zoom\-in
Zoom in.
Icon sizes step through 48, 64, 96, 168 and 256 pixels in the icon view, and
16, 32 and 64 in the details view.
Each window zooms separately, and the zoom isn't saved.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>plus\fR, \fB<Ctrl>equal\fR, \fB<Ctrl>KP_Add\fR
.TP
.B zoom\-out
Zoom out.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>minus\fR, \fB<Ctrl>KP_Subtract\fR
.TP
.B zoom\-reset
Reset zoom.
Goes back to the configured icon size.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>0\fR, \fB<Ctrl>KP_0\fR
.TP
.B location
Location.
Turns the path bar into an entry.
Type an absolute path,
.BR ~ ,
a path relative to the current folder, or a URI, and press Enter; a file
opens its folder with the file selected.
Tab completes the last part of the path, and Escape closes the entry.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>l\fR
.TP
.B toggle\-sidebar
Toggle sidebar.
.br
Keys: \fBF9\fR
.TP
.B add\-bookmark
Bookmark this folder.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>d\fR
.TP
.B sort\-by\-name
Sort by name.
Folders always come first.
Names sort naturally, so
.B file2
comes before
.BR file10 ,
and case is ignored.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B sort\-by\-size
Sort by size.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B sort\-by\-modified
Sort by modified.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B sort\-by\-type
Sort by type.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B sort\-reversed
Reverse sort order.
.br
Keys: none
.TP
.B show\-help
Keyboard shortcuts.
Shows the bindings in effect; the next key or click closes the overlay.
.br
Keys: \fBquestion\fR
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/config.ini
(usually
.IR ~/.config/junk\-drawer/config.ini )
when Junk Drawer starts; restart it to apply changes.
The file uses GLib key-file (INI) syntax and every key is optional.
Key bindings live in a second file,
.IR keybindings.ini ,
next to it (see
.BR "KEY BINDINGS" ).
.PP
When either file is missing, Junk Drawer creates it on start, listing every
setting or binding at its default but commented out: remove the leading
.B #
from a line and edit it.
A file that already exists is never written to, even when it is a symlink, so
files from dotfiles or home-manager are safe.
A file that can't be read is reported on standard error and the defaults are
used.
The same examples, with the values live, are installed as
.I share/doc/junk\-drawer/config.example.ini
and
.IR share/doc/junk\-drawer/keybindings.example.ini .
.SS [appearance]
.TP
.B flavor
The colour scheme, a Catppuccin flavor:
.BR latte ,
.BR frappe ,
.B macchiato
or
.BR mocha ,
or
.B gtk
to follow the GTK theme.
An unknown flavor falls back to mocha.
.IP
With
.BR gtk ,
the colours come from the GTK theme, such as Stylix's
.I ~/.config/gtk\-4.0/gtk.css
or adw\-gtk3: the window background and text colours, with the shades
between them mixed in Catppuccin's proportions, and the theme's accent colour.
The theme is read when Junk Drawer starts.
The accent names in
.IR style.css ,
such as \fB@mauve\fR and \fB@red\fR, keep their mocha values.
.br
Default: \fBmocha\fR
.TP
.B accent
The Catppuccin accent colour, used for the selection, focus and highlights:
rosewater, flamingo, pink, mauve, red, maroon, peach, yellow, green, teal, sky,
sapphire, blue or lavender.
An unknown accent falls back to mauve.
Ignored when
.B flavor
is
.BR gtk .
.br
Default: \fBmauve\fR
.TP
.B opacity
The opacity of the window background, from 0.0 to 1.0, so the compositor's
wallpaper or blur shows through.
.br
Default: \fB0.85\fR
.SS [view]
.TP
.B default
The view new windows start in:
.B icons
or
.BR details .
.br
Default: \fBicons\fR
.TP
.B show\-hidden
Whether new windows show hidden and backup files.
.br
Default: \fBfalse\fR
.TP
.B icon\-size
The icon size in the icon view, in pixels, from 16 to 512.
.br
Default: \fB96\fR
.TP
.B list\-icon\-size
The icon size in the details view, in pixels, from 16 to 128.
.br
Default: \fB32\fR
.TP
.B show\-path
Whether to show the path bar and its up button above the files.
.br
Default: \fBtrue\fR
.TP
.B grid\-caption
The line under each name in the icon view:
.B size
(item counts for folders),
.BR modified ,
.BR type ,
.B permissions
or
.BR none .
.br
Default: \fBsize\fR
.TP
.B show\-sidebar
Whether windows start with the sidebar shown.
.br
Default: \fBtrue\fR
.TP
.B show\-thumbnails
Whether to show thumbnails in place of icons (see
.BR THUMBNAILS ).
.br
Default: \fBtrue\fR
.TP
.B remember
Whether to remember the view, sort, hidden files, sidebar and zoom between
sessions, in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/junk\-drawer/state.ini .
With \fBfalse\fR that file is neither read nor written, and every window starts
from the values in
.IR config.ini .
.br
Default: \fBtrue\fR
.SS style.css
Extra GTK CSS is read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/style.css
after Junk Drawer's own style, so its rules win.
It can use the palette's colour names:
.BR @base ,
.BR @mantle ,
.BR @text ,
.BR @mauve
and the rest of the flavor, plus
.B @accent
and
.B @bg
(the window background at the configured opacity).
Junk Drawer's own rules are all under
.BR window.junk ,
for example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
window.junk .sidebar { background: alpha(@crust, 0.6); }
.fi
.RE
.SH THUMBNAILS
When
.B show\-thumbnails
is on, regular local files that have a thumbnail show it in place of their
icon in both views, scaled to fit and keeping its shape.
Thumbnails follow the freedesktop Thumbnail Managing Standard, so they are
shared with Nautilus and other applications.
.PP
Thumbnails are made in the background, at most two at a time, for the items
on screen, newest first; an item keeps its icon until its thumbnail is ready.
Items scrolled away or in a folder you have left are skipped.
.SS Cache
Thumbnails live in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/normal/
(128 pixels) and
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/large/
(256 pixels), named by the MD5 sum of the file's URI.
Junk Drawer uses the large size when the icon size times the display scale is over
128 pixels, and the normal size otherwise.
A cached thumbnail is used as long as its
.B Thumb::MTime
matches the file's modification time; when the file changes, a new one is
made.
.SS Making thumbnails
For a file with no current thumbnail, Junk Drawer runs the first thumbnailer whose
.B MimeType
list has the file's content type.
Thumbnailers are
.I *.thumbnailer
files in
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/thumbnailers
and in the
.I thumbnailers
folder of each directory in
.IR $XDG_DATA_DIRS .
When two directories have a file with the same name, the earlier one wins.
In the entry's
.B Exec
line,
.B %i
is the file's path,
.B %u
its URI,
.B %o
the output PNG,
.B %s
the size in pixels and
.B %%
a literal %.
The list of thumbnailers is read once, when the first thumbnail is needed.
.PP
When no thumbnailer handles the type, or the thumbnailer fails, Junk Drawer decodes
the file itself with GdkPixbuf if it can load that image type and the file is
at most 50 MB.
Bigger files are left to thumbnailers.
.PP
New thumbnails are saved, readable only by you, with
.B Thumb::URI
and
.BR Thumb::MTime .
Files inside the thumbnail cache never get thumbnails.
.SS Failures
When a thumbnailer or the decoder fails, Junk Drawer records it in
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/fail/junk\-drawer/
and doesn't try that file again until it changes.
Types that nothing can handle aren't recorded, so a thumbnailer installed later
is used straight away.
.SS Adding a thumbnailer
Install a package that ships
.I share/thumbnailers/*.thumbnailer
files, then restart Junk Drawer.
For example, ffmpegthumbnailer handles video, evince or papers handle PDF, and
libgsf handles office documents.
On NixOS, adding the package to
.B environment.systemPackages
or
.B home.packages
is enough, because both profiles link
.IR share/thumbnailers .
.SS Clearing the cache
To try failed files again, remove
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/fail/junk\-drawer
and restart Junk Drawer (it remembers thumbnails it has loaded until it exits).
Removing
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails
clears every application's thumbnails, which are then made again as needed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/config.ini
Settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/keybindings.ini
Key bindings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/junk\-drawer/style.css
Extra GTK CSS.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gtk\-3.0/bookmarks
The sidebar's bookmarks, shared with Nautilus and the GTK file chooser.
Each line is a URI, optionally followed by a space and a label.
Junk Drawer watches it, so changes from other applications show at once.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user\-dirs.dirs
The XDG user folders (Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures, Videos)
listed in the sidebar.
A folder that is unset, missing or the same as your home is left out.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/junk\-drawer/state.ini
What Junk Drawer remembers between sessions: the view, sort, hidden files,
sidebar and zoom sizes.
Remembered values override the matching settings in
.IR config.ini .
Junk Drawer writes this file; delete it to go back to the
.I config.ini
values.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/
Thumbnails; see
.BR THUMBNAILS .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/recently\-used.xbel
The files listed in Recent, which needs gvfs.
Removing an item from Recent never touches the file.
.TP
.I share/doc/junk\-drawer/config.example.ini
Every setting with its default.
.TP
.I share/junk\-drawer/org.freedesktop.FileManager1.service
The D-Bus activation file; see
.BR D-BUS .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings, bookmarks and user folders are read; default
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where thumbnails are kept; default
.IR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Searched first for thumbnailers, and holds the Recent list; default
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_DIRS
Searched for thumbnailers, desktop entries and MIME data.
.SH D-BUS
While Junk Drawer runs it owns
.B org.freedesktop.FileManager1
on the session bus, waiting in line if another file manager has it.
Its
.BR ShowFolders ,
.B ShowItems
and
.B ShowItemProperties
methods are what \(lqShow in folder\(rq in browsers and other applications
calls: they open windows on the folders, select the items, or show their
properties.
.PP
To have D-Bus start Junk Drawer for these calls when it isn't running, link the
activation file into a
.I dbus\-1/services
directory.
Nautilus ships one for the same name, so the package doesn't install it there.
The NixOS and home-manager modules do it with
.BR programs.junk\-drawer.fileManager1 ,
which is on by default when
.B programs.junk\-drawer.defaultFileManager
is.
